$NetBSD$

Audio playback on NetBSD goes through the ALSA OSS plugin provided
by alsa-plugins-oss, which routes output to /dev/dsp. To enable it,
copy the example configuration shipped by that package:

	cp /usr/pkg/share/examples/alsa-plugins-oss/asoundrc ~/.asoundrc

(or merge its contents into an existing ~/.asoundrc). The kernel
must provide a legacy OSS device (/dev/dsp or /dev/audio).
